-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:48c52af5502f483389775105c3a8c4e69cb38612c13c0f46300631a0ea90d4b9","file":"preprints/The-Bass-trace-conjecture-for-complex-group-rings-September-24-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex","line":98,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"e2a7f79f912eebe8cf345e7f69a07a0f479bae74718eadca218471a707585b09","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/The-Bass-trace-conjecture-for-complex-group-rings-September-24-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:48c52af5502f483389775105c3a8c4e69cb38612c13c0f46300631a0ea90d4b9","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/The-Bass-trace-conjecture-for-complex-group-rings-September-24-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex#L98"},"statement_kind":"corollary","text":"\\label{cor:torsion-free}\nLet $G$ be any torsion-free discrete group.\n\\begin{enumerate}[label=\\textup{(\\roman*)}]\n \\item For every $q\\geq1$ and every idempotent $e\\in M_q(\\C G)$,\n \\[\n  \\tau_{G,q}(e)=\\operatorname{rank}_{\\C}\\bigl(\\epsilon_{G,q}(e)\\bigr).\n \\]\n Consequently $\\tau_{G,*}=\\operatorname{rk}_{\\epsilon}$, with\n $\\Z$ viewed as a subgroup of $\\C$, and\n \\[\n  \\tau_{G,*}\\bigl(K_0(\\C G)\\bigr)=\\Z.\n \\]\n \\item For every commutative unital domain $R$ of characteristic zero,\n every $e\\in RG$ satisfying $e^2=e$ is either $0$ or $1$.\n\\end{enumerate}"}
